: New York Athletic Club, Chicago Athletic Association, and Missouri Athletic Club.  The New York AC defeated Missouri 5-0, and Chicago 6-0.  A fourth team tried to enter representing Germany.  However, the Germans were not allowed to compete because their athletes did not represent a single club.  This discrimination should probably eliminate water polo as an Olympic event in 1904, but it is still recognized by the " [:a {:href "/organizations/1"} "IOC"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "A sad footnote did occur after the water polo event.  The artificial lake created in the middle of the World’s Fair for the life-saving exhibition was also used for some of the agricultural exhibits, and many of the cattle at the exhibits grazed in and wandered into the lake.  Although the " [:a {:href "/editions/3/sports/SWM"} "swimming"] " and water polo events were held at the other end of the lake from the cattle, before the middle of 1905, less than one year after the water polo events in the lake, four of the water poloists died from typhus."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button127687", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button127687').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "collapse", :data-target ".team-members-558134"} [:div {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-plus"}]] [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "New York Athletic Club"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "11"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-members-558134 collapse", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [